# calc_gnd_bounce.py  CALCULATION (T-073, C2-005) on hardware/frutamidi.kicad_pcb (KiCad 10.0.4)
GND path lengths (MEASUREMENT, design file): J2 pad 1 (GND terminal) -> Pico pin 23 21.99 mm; module GND pin -> Pico pin 23 30.90 mm; shared section from node (27.00,45.60) to pin 23 3.84 mm
Arc entry: E pad -> edge track (y = 68.00) -> J2 pad 1: up to 65.2 mm (E11); this section and the trunk to the node are common to module and Pico (whole-board rise, no differential at IC pins)

IEC 61000-4-2 4 kV contact (SOURCE EE-S16 from memory, upper tolerance): Ipk 17.2 A, tr 0.6-1.0 ns, I(30 ns) 8 A
case (ASSUMPTION)                   L_diff nH di/dt A/ns  Vb peak V   I2C peak A     I2C Q nC
0.7 nH/mm, pin 3 nH, tr 0.6 ns            5.7       23.0        131         0.59         0.35
0.7 nH/mm, pin 3 nH, tr 1.0 ns            5.7       13.8         78         0.35         0.35
0.7 nH/mm, pin 10 nH, tr 0.6 ns          12.7       23.0        292         1.32         0.79
0.7 nH/mm, pin 10 nH, tr 1.0 ns          12.7       13.8        175         0.79         0.79
1.0 nH/mm, pin 3 nH, tr 0.6 ns            6.8       23.0        157         0.71         0.42
1.0 nH/mm, pin 3 nH, tr 1.0 ns            6.8       13.8         94         0.42         0.42
1.0 nH/mm, pin 10 nH, tr 0.6 ns          13.8       23.0        318         1.44         0.86
1.0 nH/mm, pin 10 nH, tr 1.0 ns          13.8       13.8        191         0.86         0.86

Worst case: module GND - Pico GND bounce 318 V for ~1 ns; after the first peak (slope to I(30 ns)) 4.3 V
  through R15/R16 (220 ohm, then the BSS138 level shifters on the module): <= 1.44 A, <= 0.86 nC per line
  RP2040 HBM 4 kV (SOURCE EE-S28, stated for digital FT pins only) = 2.67 A peak, 400 nC -> injected charge 0.2 % of the HBM charge, peak 0.54x the HBM peak
  NOT CONFIRMED: GP26/GP27 (I2C1 on the PCB) are ADC-capable pins; the extracted RP2040 table gives HBM 4 kV for FT pins and CDM 500 V, no separate HBM value for these pins was found (EE-S28)
  without the arc (strike through Rx into the MPR121 pin): pin current 1.20 A (R 3k0 + 330 ohm source, CALCULATION), bounce scaled by 0.07 -> 22 V
DECISION INPUT: the 1.40 mm gap acts as a spark gap to GND at every terminal; it keeps the strike off the MPR121 pin; residual risk = 318 V / ~1 ns GND bounce between module and Pico (ASSUMPTION-based), not measured
